5. YOUR DATA AND THIRD-PARTY SERVICES

  (a) Data you create with the Software (notes, financial records, and any
      file you choose to open) belongs to you. It is stored on your device.
      Cambric does not receive it.

  (b) The Software has no account system, no analytics, and no telemetry.

  (c) The update check contacts GitHub (api.github.com) to read the latest
      release number. It sends no personal data beyond the request itself,
      and GitHub's own privacy terms apply to that request.

  (d) The HTTP tester sends a request only to the address you enter. That
      request goes to the server you chose, not to Cambric.

6. TOOL RESULTS

The Software reports what it observes and calculates; it does not guarantee an
outcome. Financial figures are estimates for planning, not financial advice. A
clean antivirus result means the scanner found nothing, not that a file is
safe. Overwriting a file does not guarantee that it is unrecoverable on flash
storage or copy-on-write filesystems. Verify anything that matters before
acting on it.

